  "interpretation": "Branch-only Peri-RMS historically fitted recall training to 99% in all seeds but remained at 39-43% held-out after 30000 updates. Square-sum fitted training to 100% and reached about 98.72-98.79% held-out at 100000 updates, narrowly missing the first-99 criterion. Embedding normalization recovered all six misses. The initialization scale probe supports amplitude balance as a contributing hypothesis; embedding normalization also changes gradients, so the intervention does not establish a unique causal mechanism or permanent impossibility of later grokking."
